sig UD1.14 4FUF 2
# Entry PROM A1, inputs and outputs. These sit on the flow band numbered "2" with no
# test name of their own; Battlezone's sheet calls them 2A (and the counter column 2B).
sig UA1.14 F722 2
sig UA1.13 C4P5 2
sig UA1.12 6UAC 2
sig UA1.11 3441 2
sig UA1.10 2P61 2
sig UA1.9 92F3 2
sig UA1.7 A856 2
sig UA1.6 3050 2
sig UA1.5 H8F9 2
sig UA1.4 9569 2
sig UA1.3 3U53 2
sig UA1.2 9F47 2
# 4FUF: the 2nd printing writes AFUF here (and 4FUF in the TEST #2 box)
sig UA1.1 4FUF 2
# Data bus, printed on the EDB lines right of the bow-ties, flow band "3"
sig UE2.39 1441 3
sig UE2.38 2883 3
sig UE2.37 5107 3
sig UE2.36 A20P 3
sig UJ2.39 441H 3
sig UJ2.38 883A 3
sig UJ2.37 1074 3
sig UJ2.36 20P9 3

# ===========================================================================
# High Score Memory
# ===========================================================================
#
# Source: DP-190 sheet 3 Side B, 4th printing (ad5d39e0e6ea), 300 dpi tiles r2-r4 c1-c3
# and 600 dpi crops. Box spans roughly sheet x 1457-4107, y 3497-6330
# (300 dpi). Cross-checked against the 2nd printing (ba4e9f648414) everywhere and the
# 1st printing (a2e9aa09a858) at the analogue section, A3/J3/C3, H3/F3 and E3's enables.
# The three printings agree on every connection here except K3 (see the QUERY there).
# No signature-analysis annotations (blue) fall inside this box.
#
# Parts drawn in this box:
# part UA3 74LS174
# part UJ3 74LS175
# part UC3 ER2055 (64 x 8 EAROM)
# part UE3 74LS244
# part UH3 74LS244
# part UF3 74LS374
# part UF4 74LS14 (one inverter here, pins 9 -> 8; the type is printed at F4's other gate in the decoder, "F4 LS14")
# part UK3 LM324
#
# Jumpers: the sheet draws three two-pad jumpers (a pair of half-circles), undesignated.
# A bar across the pads = fitted; bare pads = open. Named JP1-JP3 here (ours).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EAROM supply: -28V from a charge pump on -22V
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A 3 kHz square from the game PCB is AC-coupled into K3, an LM324 used as a comparator
# (the 4th printing parallels all four sections). K3 runs between GND (pin 4) and -22V
# (pin 11), so its output swings ~0 V to ~-22 V. C19/CR4/CR3/C21 pump that to about
# -43 V; R27 and the 33 V zener CR2, referenced to +5V, regulate it to -28V for the
# ER2055's VEE (C3 pin 14). No transistors in this section.
net 3KHZ: J17.6 C11.1
# Uncertain: K3's sections. 4th printing: - inputs 9,13,2,6; + inputs 10,12,3,5; outputs
# 1,7,8,14 (all four sections in parallel). 2nd and 1st printings: 2,6 / 3,5 / 1,7 only
# (two sections; 8,9,10,12,13,14 not drawn). Read here as the 4th printing (primary).
wire C11.2 R6.1 UK3.9 UK3.13 UK3.2 UK3.6
wire R28.1 UK3.10 UK3.12 UK3.3 UK3.5
# Bias divider GND - R5 1K - node - R29 4.7K - -22V (about -3.9 V), filtered by C13
wire R5.2 R6.2 R28.2 R29.1 C13.2
net GND: R5.1 C13.1 UK3.4
# C13 is drawn + to ground (the node it filters is negative)
net -22V: R29.2 UK3.11 CR4.1 C21.1
# The paralleled outputs are drawn joined on one net: the checker's "more than one
# output drives it" is the drawing, not a misread (two outputs in the 1st/2nd printings).
wire UK3.1 UK3.7 UK3.8 UK3.14 C19.1
parallel UK3.1 UK3.7 UK3.8 UK3.14
# C19 + on the op-amp side. CR4: anode (2) on the pump node, cathode (1) on -22V.
# CR3: cathode (1) on the pump node, anode (2) on C21's negative end.
wire C19.2 CR4.2 CR3.1
# C21 is drawn + on the -22V line, - on the CR3/R27 node
wire CR3.2 C21.2 R27.1
# CR2 1N5257B (33 V zener): cathode (1) to +5V, anode (2) on -28V.
# C20 + to +5V, - on -28V. C16 .01 from -28V to ground.
net -28V: R27.2 CR2.2 C20.2 C16.1 UC3.14
net +5V: CR2.1 C20.1
net GND: C16.2
value C11 .1uF
value R5 1K
value R6 47K
value R28 47K
value R29 4.7K
value C13 47uF 25V
value C19 47uF 50V
value C21 47uF 50V
value C20 47uF 50V
value C16 .01uF
value R27 1K 1/2W
# Uncertain: CR3 and CR4 are printed "1N100" (read as IN100) in all three printings --
# recorded as printed; not a part number I can place.
value CR3 1N100
value CR4 1N100
value CR2 1N5257B

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EAROM address latch A3 (LS174), clocked by /EARWR
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EAB0-5 arrive by the address-bus arrow at the bracket left of A3. Each EAB line also
# has a short vertical stub up to a second copy of its name above A3; the stubs join
# nothing else.
net EAB5: UA3.14
net EAB4: UA3.3
net EAB3: UA3.13
net EAB2: UA3.4
net EAB1: UA3.11
net EAB0: UA3.6
net /EARWR: UA3.9 UF3.11
# "P,1" at A3 pin 1 (clear): pulled up through R1 (Power Inputs: "R1,54 1K PULLUP")
wire UA3.1 R1.1
# Latched address to the EAROM, each line pulled up 10K (R19-R25, "10K 6PL")
wire UA3.15 UC3.7 R25.1
wire UA3.2 UC3.8 R23.1
wire UA3.12 UC3.9 R22.1
wire UA3.5 UC3.10 R21.1
wire UA3.10 UC3.11 R20.1
wire UA3.7 UC3.12 R19.1
net +5V: R25.2 R23.2 R22.2 R21.2 R20.2 R19.2
value R19 10K
value R20 10K
value R21 10K
value R22 10K
value R23 10K
value R25 10K

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EAROM C3 (ER2055)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pin names as printed: 1 D3, 2 D7, 3 D6, 4 D5, 5 D4, 6 VSS, 7 A5, 8 A4, 9 A3, 10 A2,
# 11 A1, 12 A0, 13 CK, 14 VEE, 15 C1, 16 C2, 17 CS1, 18 /CS2, 19 VG1, 20 D0, 21 D1,
# 22 D2. (VG1 is lettered "VGI"; the draughtsman writes 1 as a bare stroke throughout --
# A1, CS1, D1, EAB1.) VSS is drawn to +5V, VEE to -28V.
net +5V: UC3.6
# VG1 (19) and /CS2 (18) are tied together and grounded
net GND: UC3.19 UC3.18

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EAROM control latch J3 (74LS175), clocked by /EARCON
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# J3's D inputs come from the H3-buffered data bus. Read off the wiring:
#   CK  = EDB0 (2D -> 2Q pin 7)      C2 = EDB1 (4D -> 4Q pin 15)
#   C1  = /EDB2 (3D -> /3Q pin 11)   CS1 = EDB3 (1D -> 1Q pin 2)
# Each of the four control lines is pulled up 10K (R26, R24, R9, R8, "10K 4PL").
net /EARCON: UJ3.9
net /RESET: UJ3.1
wire UH3.3 UF3.3 UJ3.4
wire UH3.18 UF3.18 UJ3.12
wire UH3.16 UF3.17 UJ3.13
wire UH3.14 UF3.14 UJ3.5
wire UJ3.2 R26.1 UC3.17
wire UJ3.15 R24.1 UC3.16
# C1 also drives F3's output enable: the write latch drives the EAROM's data pins only
# while C1 is low
wire UJ3.11 R9.1 UC3.15 UF3.1
wire UJ3.7 R8.1 UC3.13
nc UJ3.3 UJ3.10 UJ3.14 UJ3.6
net +5V: R26.2 R24.2 R9.2 R8.2
value R26 10K
value R24 10K
value R9 10K
value R8 10K

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EAROM data: write latch F3 (LS374) in, read buffer E3 (LS244) out
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each EAROM data pin is one node with its 10K pull-up (R13-R18, R11, R12, R14, R16,
# "10K 8PL"), F3's Q and E3's input. F3 is clocked by /EARWR (pin 11).
wire UC3.2 R16.1 UE3.4 UF3.5
wire UC3.3 R14.1 UE3.6 UF3.6
wire UC3.4 R12.1 UE3.8 UF3.9
wire UC3.5 R11.1 UE3.11 UF3.12
wire UC3.1 R18.1 UE3.2 UF3.2
wire UC3.22 R17.1 UE3.17 UF3.19
wire UC3.21 R15.1 UE3.15 UF3.16
wire UC3.20 R13.1 UE3.13 UF3.15
net +5V: R16.2 R14.2 R12.2 R11.2 R18.2 R17.2 R15.2 R13.2
value R11 10K
value R12 10K
value R13 10K
value R14 10K
value R15 10K
value R16 10K
value R17 10K
value R18 10K
net EDB7: UE3.16
net EDB6: UE3.14
net EDB5: UE3.12
net EDB4: UE3.9
net EDB3: UE3.18
net EDB2: UE3.3
net EDB1: UE3.5
net EDB0: UE3.7
# E3 enables: /1G (pin 1) on /EARD, which also feeds the F4 inverter. /2G (pin 19)
# reaches /EARD through JP1 (drawn fitted) or F4's inverted /EARD through JP2
# (drawn open). Same in all three printings.
net /EARD: UE3.1 UF4.9 JP1.1
wire UE3.19 JP1.2 JP2.1
wire UF4.8 JP2.2
value JP1 fitted
value JP2 open

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data-bus buffer H3 (LS244): EDB and the 3 MHz clock in, to F3/J3 and E3MHZ out
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EDB6 is not buffered: its slot on H3 (pin 13) carries the 3 MHz clock, and EDB6 runs
# round H3 straight to F3 pin 7.
net EDB7: UH3.15
net EDB5: UH3.11
net EDB4: UH3.8
net EDB3: UH3.17
net EDB2: UH3.2
net EDB1: UH3.4
net EDB0: UH3.6
net EDB6: UF3.7
wire UH3.5 UF3.4
wire UH3.9 UF3.8
wire UH3.12 UF3.13
# Uncertain: the sheet prints E3MHZ twice here -- beside the J17 pin 4 hexagon (the clock
# off the cable, terminated by R65 220 to ground) and at H3 pin 7 (the same clock
# buffered, with a test-point flag, running off as a net label). They are the two
# sides of a buffer, so they cannot be one net. The decoder (C5 pin 9) and the Math
# Box (A2 pin 2) take E3MHZ by name with no hexagon of their own, so the buffered
# side keeps the sheet's name and the cable side gets a label of ours.
label E3MHZ-IN: J17.4 R65.1 UH3.13
net GND: R65.2
value R65 220
# TP8: test-point flag labelled "E3MHZ" on H3 pin 7
net E3MHZ: UH3.7 TP8.1
# H3 enables: /1G (pin 1) grounded; /2G (pin 19) to ground through JP3 (drawn fitted),
# otherwise held high by R10 10K. R10's supply is lettered "+5V" in the 1st printing;
# the 2nd and 4th lost the vertical stroke of the + ("-5V" at a glance).
net GND: UH3.1 JP3.1
wire UH3.19 JP3.2 R10.1
net +5V: R10.2
value R10 10K
value JP3 fitted

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Named lines that leave this box (joined by name; no unnamed exits)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /EARCON: from J3 pin 9 up the left side at sheet x~1690, crosses the box top at
#   y~3497, then right along y~3405 to x~3757 and up towards the decoder.
# /EARD:   up the right side at sheet x~3901 from y~5345, through the box top.
# /EARWR:  from F3 pin 11 right along y~6085, up at x~3932 through the box top.
# /RESET:  from J3 pin 1 right along y~5410, down at x~3901, then right along y~6243
#   out through the box's right edge (x~4107) towards the Player Inputs box.
# -22V:    a label at the end of R29's wire; the rail comes in on J18 pins 4 and N
#   (Power Inputs box, C37 470 25V).
# EAB0-5:  the black address-bus arrow into A3's bracket.
# EDB0-7:  the grey data-bus arrow into H3's bracket; E3's outputs to the grey bus
#   that runs down the right of the box to the bottom bus.

# ===========================================================================
# Player Inputs and Audio Output
# ===========================================================================
#
# Source: DP-190 sheet 3 Side B, 4th printing (ad5d39e0e6ea, "037585-01 B +"),
# read from the 300 dpi tiles and 600 dpi crops. Every section was
# compared with the 2nd printing (ba4e9f648414) and the 1st (a2e9aa09a858,
# "037585-01 A", box titled "Switch Inputs & Audio Output"); they agree except
# where a QUERY says otherwise. Values were checked against the typeset parts
# list, TM-190 2nd printing Figure 22 (doc 56a2f53adedf p45-46).
#
# Extent: the box from sheet x~4205 to ~10010, y~3507 to ~6445 (300 dpi), which
# also holds the Encoder Wheel PCB inset, the NOTE legend and the NOTICE text.
# The grey EDB bus runs inside the box's right and bottom edges.
#
# Legend (NOTE box, bottom centre of this box): square = edge connector J18,
# hexagon = interconnect connection J17, circle = SA connector J16, flag = test
# point. No hexagons appear in this box. TP9 and TP10 are ours.
#
# Power pins are drawn only on the POKEYs (17 +5V, 1 GND) and on K6 (4 +22V,
# 11 GND); the build adds every other supply pin from the standard pinout.

# part UC/D2 C012294-01 (POKEY, "Audio 2" in the TM-190 self-test)
# part UB/C2 C012294-01 (POKEY, "Audio 1" in the TM-190 self-test)
# part UD6 74LS157
# part UC6 74LS74
# part UA4 74LS191
# part UE6 4584B
# part UH4 74LS174
# part UK6 LM324
# part UF4 74LS14
# part UF5 74S03
# part SW1 4-position DIP switch (66-114P1T "4-Station Bit Switch", TM-190 parts list)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Encoder Wheel PCB (A035220-01 A) -- a different board, drawn as an inset.
# None of its parts are in this netlist.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The inset shows the encoder ("coupler") PCB: two IR LEDs in series from +5V
# through its own R1 (100 ohm) to GND, and two phototransistors, collectors on
# +5V, emitters out as CLK 1 and DIR 1. Its four-pin connector is drawn with the
# same square symbol as J18 and numbered 1 CLK 1, 2 +5V, 3 GND, 4 DIR 1 -- these
# are the encoder board's own pins, NOT J18.1-4 (J18.1/J18.2 are this board's
# GND/+5V on the Power Inputs box). Its R1 is not this board's R1 (the 1K pull-up
# printed "P,R1" on the POKEYs' CS1).
# The sheet draws no wire from the inset to this board. Its signals arrive on
# J18.J, J18.8, J18.H and J18.7 below. By function: J/8 feed the direction latch
# (C6 D) and H/7 the count clock (C6 CK, A4 CK), and J/H are the mux's A inputs
# (FLIP low), 8/7 its B inputs (FLIP high, the other cocktail player). So J18.J
# and J18.H carry DIR and CLK of one encoder, J18.8 and J18.7 of the other --
# an inference from the circuit; the sheet does not label these pins.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Encoder inputs -- each: 0.1 + 3.3K to ground, AC-coupled through 1.0uF 50V
# into a 4584B Schmitt inverter biased at its own threshold through 10K
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Electrolytics: "+" is printed on the inverter side; pin 1 (+) is that side.
wire J18.J C42.1 R47.1 C46.2
wire C46.1 R52.1 UE6.13
wire J18.8 C43.1 R46.1 C45.2
wire C45.1 R51.1 UE6.11
wire J18.H C28.1 R40.1 C32.2
wire C32.1 R50.1 UE6.5
wire J18.7 C29.1 R39.1 C31.2
wire C31.1 R49.1 UE6.9
net GND: C42.2 R47.2 C43.2 R46.2 C28.2 R40.2 C29.2 R39.2
# Bias generator: E6 1->2 with R53 from output back to input and C48 to ground
# is a relaxation oscillator; R48/C47 average it to the 4584B's own switching
# threshold, and R49-R52 hold each coupled input at that level. The vertical
# bias line at x~4750 crosses the J18.8, H, 7 signal lines without dots.
wire C48.1 R48.1 R53.1 UE6.1
wire R53.2 UE6.2
wire R48.2 R49.2 R50.2 R51.2 R52.2 C47.1
net GND: C47.2 C48.2
# E6 gate 3->4 is not drawn anywhere on the sheet (checked the decoder, Math Box
# and High Score Memory boxes); the drawing leaves the CMOS inputs open.
nc UE6.3 UE6.4
value C42 .1uF
value C43 .1uF
value C28 .1uF
value C29 .1uF
value R47 3.3K
value R46 3.3K
value R40 3.3K
value R39 3.3K
value C46 1.0uF 50V
value C45 1.0uF 50V
value C32 1.0uF 50V
value C31 1.0uF 50V
value R52 10K
value R51 10K
value R50 10K
value R49 10K
value R48 10K
value R53 1K
value C48 1000pF
value C47 1.0uF 50V

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Encoder select, direction latch and up/down counter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# D6 (LS157) picks one player's encoder with FLIP: section 1 (2A/3B -> 4) is
# the direction, section 4 (14A/13B -> 12) the clock. C6 latches direction on
# the clock edge; A4 counts up or down on the same edge. The count TBC0-3 is
# read by POKEY B/C2 on P0-P3. A4's load is never asserted (LD pulled up) and
# its data inputs are grounded.
wire UE6.12 UD6.2
wire UE6.10 UD6.3
wire UE6.6 UD6.14
wire UE6.8 UD6.13
net FLIP: UD6.1
net GND: UD6.15
wire UD6.4 UC6.2
wire UD6.12 UC6.3 UA4.14
wire UC6.5 UA4.5
# "P,R54" at C6 pin 4 (preset), C6 pin 1 (clear) and A4 pin 11 (load)
wire UC6.4 UC6.1 UA4.11 R54.1
nc UC6.6
# C6's second flip-flop is not drawn anywhere on the sheet
nc UC6.8 UC6.9 UC6.10 UC6.11 UC6.12 UC6.13
net GND: UA4.4 UA4.15 UA4.1 UA4.10 UA4.9
nc UA4.12 UA4.13
net TBC0: UA4.3 UB/C2.14
net TBC1: UA4.2 UB/C2.15
net TBC2: UA4.6 UB/C2.12
net TBC3: UA4.7 UB/C2.13

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Player control panel -- each switch: 470 pull-up, 1K series, .1 to ground
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net ZAP1: J18.10 R60.1 R56.1
net ZAP2: J18.L R59.1 R55.1
net FIRE1: J18.9 R62.1 R58.1
net FIRE2: J18.K R61.1 R57.1
net +5V: R60.2 R59.2 R62.2 R61.2
# D6 section 3 (11A/10B -> 9) picks the ZAP button, section 2 (5A/6B -> 7) FIRE
wire R56.2 C53.1 UD6.11
wire R55.2 C52.1 UD6.10
wire R58.2 C50.1 UD6.5
wire R57.2 C51.1 UD6.6
net GND: C50.2 C51.2 C52.2 C53.2
wire UD6.9 UC/D2.13
wire UD6.7 UC/D2.10
value R60 470
value R59 470
value R62 470
value R61 470
value R56 1K
value R55 1K
value R57 1K
# Uncertain: the 4th printing letters R58 "15 K" (clearly, in a hand unlike the
# other three "1K"s). The 1st and 2nd printings print 1K, and the typeset TM-190
# parts list puts R58 in "1K Ohm (R1, 5, 7, 41, 45, 53-58, 64, 66-70)". 15K in
# series with an LS157 input could never pull it low, so FIRE1 would be dead.
# Recorded as 1K on the house rule (typeset beats hand-lettered).
value R58 1K
value C50 .1uF
value C51 .1uF
value C52 .1uF
value C53 .1uF

# START buttons
# The two 470 pull-ups are drawn side by side under one "+5V": the left one
# (label "R44" to its left) dots onto the START1 line and crosses START2 without
# a dot; the right one (label "R63" between the two) dots onto START2. All three
# printings draw it the same way.
net START2: J18.M R63.1 R45.1
net START1: J18.11 R44.1 R64.1
net +5V: R44.2 R63.2
wire R45.2 C40.1 UC/D2.8
wire R64.2 C55.1 UC/D2.11
net GND: C40.2 C55.2
value R44 470
value R63 470
value R45 1K
value R64 1K
value C40 .1uF
value C55 .1uF

# Cocktail-cabinet input
net /COCKTAIL: J18.C R43.1 R68.1
net +5V: R43.2
wire R68.2 C39.1 UB/C2.10
# Uncertain: the 4th printing draws C39 from the P4 node UP to its own "+5V" label.
# The 1st and 2nd printings draw C39 from the same node DOWN to a ground symbol.
# Recorded per the 4th (primary); either way it only filters the input.
net +5V: C39.2
value R43 470
value R68 1K
value C39 .1uF

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option switch D/E2 (TM-190: "Game Difficulty"), 1K pull-ups
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# P5/P2/P1/P0 are hand-lettered labels at the switch ends and again beside the
# POKEY pins (P2, P1, P0 at C/D2; P5 at B/C2). Same in all three printings.
net P5: SW1.1 R66.1 UB/C2.11
net P2: SW1.2 R70.1 UC/D2.12
net P1: SW1.3 R67.1 UC/D2.15
net P0: SW1.4 R69.1 UC/D2.14
net +5V: R66.2 R70.2 R67.2 R69.2
net GND: SW1.8 SW1.7 SW1.6 SW1.5
value R66 1K
value R70 1K
value R67 1K
value R69 1K

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# POKEY C/D2 (C012294-01) -- "Audio 2": DIP switch, ZAP, FIRE, START1, START2
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pin numbers checked against the Battlezone B/C2 POKEY and custom_pinouts.json:
# no disagreement on any pin.
net +5V: UC/D2.17
net GND: UC/D2.1
net EDB7: UC/D2.6
net EDB6: UC/D2.5
net EDB5: UC/D2.4
net EDB4: UC/D2.3
net EDB3: UC/D2.2
net EDB2: UC/D2.40
net EDB1: UC/D2.39
net EDB0: UC/D2.38
net EPHI2: UC/D2.7
net ER/WB: UC/D2.32
net /POKEY2: UC/D2.30
net EAB3: UC/D2.33
net EAB2: UC/D2.34
net EAB1: UC/D2.35
net EAB0: UC/D2.36
# CS1 printed "P,R1" on both POKEYs
wire UC/D2.31 UB/C2.31 R1.1
# SOD looped straight back to SID (no pull-up drawn, unlike Battlezone's R46)
wire UC/D2.28 UC/D2.24
# P7 is drawn as a bare stub
nc UC/D2.9
net POKAU2: UC/D2.37 R3.1 C9.1 R33.1
net +5V: R3.2
net GND: C9.2
value R3 10K
value C9 .015uF
# Keyboard scan, serial clocks and IRQ are not drawn
nc UC/D2.16 UC/D2.18 UC/D2.19 UC/D2.20 UC/D2.21 UC/D2.22 UC/D2.23 UC/D2.25 UC/D2.26 UC/D2.27 UC/D2.29

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# POKEY B/C2 (C012294-01) -- "Audio 1": encoder count, cocktail, DIP switch 1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net +5V: UB/C2.17
net GND: UB/C2.1
net EDB7: UB/C2.6
net EDB6: UB/C2.5
net EDB5: UB/C2.4
net EDB4: UB/C2.3
net EDB3: UB/C2.2
net EDB2: UB/C2.40
net EDB1: UB/C2.39
net EDB0: UB/C2.38
net EPHI2: UB/C2.7
net ER/WB: UB/C2.32
net /POKEY1: UB/C2.30
net EAB3: UB/C2.33
net EAB2: UB/C2.34
net EAB1: UB/C2.35
net EAB0: UB/C2.36
wire UB/C2.28 UB/C2.24
# P6 and P7 are drawn as bare stubs
nc UB/C2.8 UB/C2.9
net POKAU1: UB/C2.37 R4.1 C10.1 R32.1
net +5V: R4.2
net GND: C10.2
value R4 10K
value C10 .015uF
nc UB/C2.16 UB/C2.18 UB/C2.19 UB/C2.20 UB/C2.21 UB/C2.22 UB/C2.23 UB/C2.25 UB/C2.26 UB/C2.27 UB/C2.29

# Where the POKEYs' control lines come from (all named at the pins, so they join
# by name; sheet coordinates at 300 dpi):
#   EPHI2   enters through the box top running south at x~5745 (from a run along
#           y~3307), east along y~4873 to a dot at x~7140, then up to C/D2.7 and
#           down to B/C2.7. It crosses the address bus and the y~3412 line
#           without dots.
#   /POKEY2 south at x~6958 (from y~3278), east at y~4280 to C/D2.30.
#   /POKEY1 south at x~7065 (from y~3242), east at y~5680 to B/C2.30.
#   ER/WB   south at x~7108 (from y~3205), stubs east to C/D2.32 and B/C2.32.
#   EAB0-3  the thick black address-bus arrow, down x~6990-7045 from y~3340,
#           with an arrow into each POKEY's EAB3..EAB0 bracket.
#   EDB0-7  the grey data bus, arrows into each POKEY's bracket.
# The other D6 and START/ZAP/FIRE lines cross these verticals without dots.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio output -- K6 sums the two POKEYs into AUD+ and inverts it for AUD-
# ("To Regulator/Audio II PCB"; the 1st printing says "Regulator Audio Board")
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# POKAU2 and POKAU1 each cross their POKEY's SOD-SID loop without a dot.
wire R33.2 R32.2 R34.1 UK6.10
net GND: R34.2 R36.1
wire R36.2 R38.1 UK6.9
# TP9: flag labelled "AUD+"
net AUD+: UK6.8 R38.2 C27.1 TP9.1 J18.5
wire C27.2 R35.1
wire R35.2 R37.1 UK6.6
net +5V: UK6.5
# TP10: flag labelled "AUD-"
net AUD-: UK6.7 R37.2 TP10.1 J18.D
net +22V: UK6.4
# J18.6 "AUD+ RET" and J18.E "AUD- RET" are both on K6's ground
net GND: UK6.11 J18.6 J18.E
# K6's first and fourth op-amps are not drawn anywhere on the sheet (the other
# LM324, K3 in the High Score Memory, is the one with all four sections used)
nc UK6.1 UK6.2 UK6.3 UK6.12 UK6.13 UK6.14
value R33 330K
value R32 330K
value R34 22K
value R36 10K
value R38 100K
value C27 .1uF
value R35 100K
value R37 100K

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Output latch H4 (LS174) on /OL: SA enable, FLIP, the two start-button LEDs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /OL enters through the box top at x~8050 running south, east along y~5162 to
# x~8606, down to H4.9. It is named at the pin.
net /OL: UH4.9
net EDB3: UH4.6
net EDB2: UH4.11
net EDB1: UH4.13
net EDB0: UH4.14
# Circle 10 = SA connector J16 pin 10
net SAEN 2,3: UH4.7 J16.10
# FLIP runs east along y~5730 to x~9327, down to y~6285, west along the bottom
# of the box (crossing the /RESET run and under the grey bus at x~8030-8100
# without dots) to x~5180 and up to D6.1. Nothing else taps it.
net FLIP: UH4.10
wire UH4.12 R30.1
wire UH4.15 R31.1
net START LED1: R30.2 J18.12
net START LED2: R31.2 J18.13
value R30 150
value R31 150
# D1 and D2 (pins 3, 4) and Q1, Q2 (pins 2, 5) are drawn as bare stubs, in all
# three printings: the latch's first two flip-flops are unused.
nc UH4.2 UH4.3 UH4.4 UH4.5
# /RESET from J18.F clears H4 and leaves the box heading west along y~6242,
# crossing the box's left edge at x~4205 (to J3.1 in the High Score Memory,
# which names it /RESET too).
net /RESET: J18.F UH4.1 R7.1
net +5V: R7.2
value R7 1K

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Math Box status read: /STREN gates STOP onto EDB7
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /STREN enters through the box top at x~8087 running south, east along y~5125
# to x~9108, down to F4.13. STOP is a label at F5.10 (driven in the Math Box).
# F5.8 is open collector, pulled up by R41; the EDB7 label carries an arrow down
# into the grey data bus.
net /STREN: UF4.13
wire UF4.12 UF5.9
net STOP: UF5.10
net EDB7: UF5.8 R41.1
net +5V: R41.2
value R41 1K
# F4's other inverters (1->2, 5->6, 9->8, 11->10) and F5's other gates (1-3,
# 4-6) are drawn in the other boxes; their pins are theirs to account for.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lines in this box that touch nothing here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A long horizontal at y~3412, between the Math Box and this box's top edge
# (y~3507): from x~3935 (the High Score reader's /EARWR, going up through their
# box top at x~3932) east to x~10010, under the grey bus, then north up the
# sheet's right edge. It has no junction in the Player Inputs box, so it joins nothing.
# No unnamed wire crosses this box's boundary: every line that does is named at
# its pin here (EPHI2, ER/WB, /POKEY1, /POKEY2, EAB0-3, /OL, /STREN, /RESET),
# a bus (EDB, EAB), or a "P,R" pull-up reference (R1.1, R54.1).

# ===========================================================================
# Pins the sheet does not draw anywhere
# ===========================================================================
# Every box was read gate by gate, and none of them draws these. Unused as far as the
# drawing says; a spare gate's inputs may still be tied somewhere on the PCB that the
# schematic does not show.
# A2's second flip-flop (the LS109's pins 9-15)
nc UA2.9 UA2.10 UA2.11 UA2.12 UA2.13 UA2.14 UA2.15
# E4's first AND, E5's first two XORs, F5's first NAND
nc UE4.1 UE4.2 UE4.3
nc UE5.1 UE5.2 UE5.3 UE5.4 UE5.5 UE5.6
nc UF5.1 UF5.2 UF5.3
# J16 is a 12-pin header (TM-190 parts list); the sheet draws circles 1 and 3-10 only
nc J16.2 J16.11 J16.12

# ===========================================================================
# Names for the parts the sheet does not designate (shown as their values)
# ===========================================================================
value J16 SA header
value J17 Interconnect
value J18 Edge connector
value SW1 4-position DIP switch (D/E2)
value TP1 EPHI2
value TP2 ER/WB
value TP3 +5V
value TP4 GND
value TP5 -22V
value TP6 +22V
value TP7 E6MHZ
value TP8 E3MHZ
value TP9 AUD+
value TP10 AUD-
